//@version=4
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// OpenPineScript golden-data harness — BUILT-INS THAT DO NOT EXIST BEFORE v4.
//
// TradingView added these in March 2020: bb, bbw, kc, kcw, dmi, wpr, hma,
// supertrend, cmo, mfi, plus the variables iii, wvad, wad, obv, pvt, nvi, pvi.
// A v3 script calling any of them fails to compile —
//
//     Could not find function or function reference 'bb'
//
// — which is why they live here and not in ../v3/. Only the three this engine
// actually implements are plotted; adding a call to one it does not implement
// would fail locally rather than tell us anything about TradingView.
//
// HOW THIS ONE IS COMPARED
//
// It is compiled AS v4, by the v4 pipeline, because the golden test now takes
// each harness's version from its directory.
//
// That was not always so. While this engine implemented v1–v3 only, every
// harness was forced through the v3 pipeline — which still tested the
// arithmetic, since the runtime is shared across versions by design
// (dev-docs/00-architecture-assessment.md §5.6), but said nothing about whether
// v4 resolved these names at all. Now both are tested.
//
// Convergent, so the standard warm-up allowance applies.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
study(title="OPS golden v4 builtins", shorttitle="OPS v4", overlay=false)

src = close

[bbMid, bbUpper, bbLower] = bb(src, 20, 2)
plot(bbMid,   title="bb_mid")
plot(bbUpper, title="bb_upper")
plot(bbLower, title="bb_lower")

plot(wpr(14),      title="wpr_14")
plot(mfi(src, 14), title="mfi_14")

// Plotted alongside so a disagreement separates "our bb is wrong" from "our sma
// or stdev is wrong" — the manual form in ../v3/harness_bands.pine must agree
// with the built-in form here.
plot(sma(src, 20),                    title="bb_mid_manual")
plot(sma(src, 20) + 2 * stdev(src, 20), title="bb_upper_manual")
plot(sma(src, 20) - 2 * stdev(src, 20), title="bb_lower_manual")
